        <h1>Privacy Policy</h1>
        <p class="legal-date">Last updated: August 25, 2026</p>
        <p>This policy explains how VitalReach Wellness Hub collects, uses, stores, and shares information when you visit our website, contact us, submit a purchase inquiry, or use the restricted administration portal.</p>
    </header>

    <section>
        <h2>1. Who we are</h2>
        <p>VitalReach Wellness Hub is a Ghanaian-American wellness brand providing wellness products and health education. References to “VitalReach,” “we,” “us,” or “our” in this policy mean VitalReach Wellness Hub.</p>
        <address>
            <b>VitalReach Wellness Hub</b>
            <br />24 Kusia Street<br />Kokomlemle, Accra, Ghana<br />
            <a href="/contact?message=Hello%20VitalReach%2C%0A%0AI%20have%20a%20question%20about%20the%20VitalReach%20privacy%20policy.%0A%0AThank%20you.">hello@vitalreachwellness.com</a>
            <br />
            <a href="tel:+14105044449">(410) 504-4449</a>
        </address>
    </section>

    <section>
        <h2>2. Information we collect</h2>
        <h3>Information you provide</h3>
        <p>If you contact us or send a purchase inquiry, we receive the information you include, such as your name, email address, telephone number, requested products, delivery information, and message. The current website does not collect card or bank-account information and does not process online payments.</p>
        <h3>Google administrator sign-in</h3>
        <p>The administration portal is restricted to approved users. When an administrator signs in with Google, VitalReach accesses the basic identity information needed to authenticate and authorize that user: Google account email address, name, profile identifier, and authentication status. We do not request access to Gmail, Google Drive, contacts, calendars, passwords, or other Google account content.</p>
        <h3>Technical information</h3>
        <p>Our hosting systems may record standard technical data such as IP address, browser and device type, requested pages, timestamps, referring page, and security or error events. This information is used to operate, secure, and troubleshoot the website.</p>
    </section>

    <section>
        <h2>3. How we use information</h2>
        <ul>
            <li>Respond to questions, product inquiries, and partnership requests.</li>
            <li>Prepare and fulfill requested orders when ordering becomes available.</li>
            <li>Authenticate approved administrators and enforce the administrator access list.</li>
            <li>Maintain product information and website operations.</li>
            <li>Detect abuse, investigate security incidents, and protect our systems.</li>
            <li>Meet legal, regulatory, accounting, or safety obligations.</li>
        </ul>
    </section>

    <section>
        <h2>4. Google user data</h2>
        <p>Google user data is used only to sign an approved administrator into the VitalReach administration portal, display their identity within that portal, and record who made administrative changes. Access is limited to users whose email addresses are active in our administrator database.</p>
        <p>We do not sell Google user data, use it for advertising, or share it with unrelated third parties. Authentication is provided by Google, and Google’s own handling of information is governed by the <a href="https://policies.google.com/privacy" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Google Privacy Policy</a>.</p>
    </section>

    <section>
        <h2>5. Cookies and authentication</h2>
        <p>We use essential cookies for administrator authentication, security, and interactive website functionality. These cookies are not used to build advertising profiles. Administrator authentication cookies are HTTP-only, transmitted securely over HTTPS, and configured to expire after a limited period of inactivity.</p>
    </section>

    <section>
        <h2>6. When information may be shared</h2>
        <p>We may share information with service providers that support website hosting, authentication, email, security, or order fulfillment, but only as needed to provide those services. We may also disclose information when required by law, to protect people or property, or in connection with a legitimate business reorganization. We do not sell personal information.</p>
    </section>

    <section>
        <h2>7. Retention and security</h2>
        <p>We retain information only for as long as reasonably necessary for the purposes described in this policy, including operational, legal, accounting, and security needs. Administrator access records remain until they are removed or are no longer needed for security and audit purposes.</p>
        <p>We use measures such as HTTPS, restricted server access, key-based administration, access controls, and protected authentication cookies. No method of storage or transmission is completely secure, so we cannot guarantee absolute security.</p>
    </section>

    <section>
        <h2>8. Your choices and rights</h2>
        <p>You may ask us to access, correct, or delete personal information you provided, subject to applicable law and legitimate retention requirements. Administrators may also request removal from the portal access list. Send requests through our <a href="/contact?message=Hello%20VitalReach%2C%0A%0AI%20would%20like%20to%20submit%20a%20privacy%20request.%20The%20details%20of%20my%20request%20are%3A%0A%0A">contact form</a>. We may need to verify your identity before completing a request.</p>
    </section>

    <section>
        <h2>9. Children’s privacy</h2>
        <p>The website and administration portal are not directed to children under 13, and we do not knowingly collect personal information from children under 13. Contact us if you believe a child has provided information to us.</p>
    </section>

    <section>
        <h2>10. International use</h2>
        <p>VitalReach serves communities in Ghana and the United States. Information may be processed in countries where we or our service providers operate. Applicable privacy protections may differ between jurisdictions.</p>
    </section>

    <section>
        <h2>11. External links and health information</h2>
        <p>Our website may link to independent websites, including Google and health-information resources. Their privacy practices are governed by their own policies. VitalReach health content is educational and is not a substitute for professional medical advice, diagnosis, or treatment.</p>
    </section>

    <section>
        <h2>12. Policy updates</h2>
        <p>We may update this policy as our services or legal obligations change. The revised version will be posted here with a new “Last updated” date. Material changes may also be communicated through the website or directly to affected users when appropriate.</p>
    </section>

    <section>
        <h2>13. Contact us</h2>
        <p>Questions or privacy requests may be sent through our <a href="/contact?message=Hello%20VitalReach%2C%0A%0AI%20have%20a%20privacy%20question%20or%20request.%0A%0AThank%20you.">contact form</a> or mailed to VitalReach Wellness Hub, 24 Kusia Street, Kokomlemle, Accra, Ghana.</p>
    </section>
